| Have you been to the Gnomish Mines yet?  If not I'd head back up and do
| the mines.  You can strip some good armor off the corpses of all the
| gnomes, dwarves etc. you will meet there.  If you happen to have
| 400 X experience level gold, offering it to the priest in the GM temple
| could help with your AC problem.  Any priest will do; it doesn't have to
| be a like-aligned priest.

Are you quite sure about this?  I've tried to give most of the Ludios
spoils to a non-aligned priest, but I didn't notice anything except
for 'I thank thee for thy contribution' from the priest.  I think it
was in 3.1.1 and it happened some time ago so maybe I'm missing
something.  However, in my 3.0 spoiler file it is stated that the
priest should be co-aligned.

| : I am looking for a a polymorph wand as my first priority item but am I
| : wrong? Suppose I get a wish from a potion or so. What should I do??

| I wouldn't attach so much importance to polypiling.  That pile of stuff
| won't go anywhere except for food items.

Thats not entirely true.  A lot of monsters have become quite
intelligent in 3.1.  Generally these monsters will pick up weapons,
armor, food, gems, and certain wands, potions, and scrolls, and use
them against YOU.  I actually think that this can be used for
identification of wands, potions, and scrolls: the dwarf wont care
about it if it hasn't got any offensive or defensive capabilities.  So
wands of magic missile, potions of healing, and scrolls of teleport
will be picked up, but not wands of secret door detection, potions of
object detection, or scrolls of identify.  All this is in fact wild
guesswork based on observation during a lot of games - I havn't looked
into the code.

Anyway, I once was gathering piles of stuff in a room (my base camp).
I was careful about closing and maybe even locking doors leading into
this room so no monster could enter.  Suddenly, while tending to other
business in the temple on the same level 'You hear a door open'.  Put
on the blindfold to see the new monster.  Oops, an ogre in my base
camp.  Hurry up, have to kill him.  When I got to the ogre he had
already been walking around in the room picking up various stuff.
Then I blasted him with Mjollnir to get my stuff back.  Loosing a lot
of HP he promptly read a scroll of teleportation - oh, no!  It was
from my pile of cursed scrolls of teleportation for use later in the
game.  Away goes the ogre with lots of my stuff to another level.
Later I found him way down in the dungeons and I killed him before he
could escape - phew!

